":"text","text":"relative accuracy under any weight spread. O(n³) time, n² "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Double"},{"type":"text","text":"s."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"sections":[],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The Kemeny constant: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"transition rates, a loop taken with probability 2w\/d(v)) from a vertex to a target drawn"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"from the stationary distribution, which does not depend on the start; Σ_{i≥2} 1\/μᵢ over the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"normalized Laplacian spectrum. nil when the graph is not connected, 0 for zero or one vertex."}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kemenyConstant()","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"references":{"doc://SpectralGraphTheory/documentation/SpectralGraphTheory/GraphProtocols/Graph/kemenyConstant()":{"url":"\/documentation\/spectralgraphtheory\/graphprotocols\/graph\/kemenyconstant()","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpectralGraphTheory\/documentation\/SpectralGraphTheory\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/kemenyConstant()","type":"topic","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"The Kemeny constant: the expected number of steps of the random walk (edge weights as","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"transition rates, a loop taken with probability 2w\/d(v)) from a vertex to a target drawn","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"from the stationary distribution, which does not depend on the start; Σ_{i≥2} 1\/μᵢ over the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text